Create a self-contained prompt that instructs an AI coding agent to write a
Python script with the following specification: Write a single-file Python
script (Termux-compatible, with a `/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/env
python` shebang) that converts PDF files into JPEG images, one folder per PDF,
using the `pdf2image` library.
The script should begin with `from __future__ import annotations` and import
`shutil`, `pathlib.Path`, and `convert_from_path` from `pdf2image`.
Define a module-level constant `POPPLER_PATH` set to `None` so users can point
it at a Poppler binary directory if needed.
Implement a function `convert_pdf_to_jpg(pdf_path: Path, output_folder: Path) ->
bool` with these behaviors: - Print a progress line naming the PDF file (name
only, not full path) before converting. - Create a subfolder inside
`output_folder` named after the PDF's stem (filename without extension),
creating parent directories as needed and tolerating an existing folder. - Call
`convert_from_path` with 300 DPI, JPEG format, 4 threads, the per-PDF subfolder
as the output folder, and `POPPLER_PATH` as the Poppler path. - Note that
`convert_from_path` writes files named with a `jpeg` extension using the pattern
`<stem>_page_<n>.jpeg` (1-based page numbers).
For each returned page, locate that expected file in the subfolder; if it
exists, rename it to a `.jpg` extension with the same stem and page number using
`shutil.move`, and record it.
If it does not exist, print a warning naming the expected path and continue. -
After processing, print a success message stating how many JPG files were
produced and the output directory. - Return `True` on success.
Wrap the whole operation in a broad `try/except Exception`; on error, print an
error message identifying the PDF file name and the exception, and return
`False`.
The script should also include a `main` entry point (guarded by `if __name__ ==
"__main__":`) that performs the batch workflow: it should accept or determine a
source directory containing PDFs and an output directory, iterate over all
`.pdf` files, call `convert_pdf_to_jpg` for each, and report a summary of
successes and failures.
Use `pathlib` for all path handling.
Handle the case where no PDFs are found by printing a clear message rather than
failing silently.
Use `print` for all user-facing output (no logging framework required).
Usage and environment notes: the script targets Termux on Android, so
`pdf2image` requires the Poppler utilities (`pdftoppm`) to be installed in the
environment; if `POPPLER_PATH` is `None`, Poppler must be on the system PATH.
Keep the code dependency-light, standard-library-plus-`pdf2image` only, and
avoid any non-essential features.
Use type hints throughout and match the terse, readable style of a small utility
script. ---
